PRIVATE REFLECTION: Round 2 public responses strongly solidified the core travel-dash-with-on-arrival damage/CC set and kept the same exclusion pattern for pure mobility/teleport.

Core unanimous / high-consensus yes for dash-Flash buffering the dash’s own hit:
Gragas E Rolling Corkscrew knock-up, Vi Q Vault Breaker stun, Jarvan E Dragon Strike stun/damage, Fizz E Playful Trickster damage on arrival, Galio E Winds of War/Heroic Charge stun, Kayn Q Dark Reaping/Reaped Shadows/Umbral Dash damage on arrival, Poppy E Heroic Charge stun, Pyke E Bone Skewer silence/damage on arrival, Rell W Ferrous Charge/Shattering Strike stun, Riven Q3 Broken Wings damage/knock-up, Sejuani Q Arctic Assault/Permafrost charge knock-up, Tryndamere E Spinning Slash damage on arrival, Yone Q3 Spirit Cleave damage, Zac E Elastic Slingshot knock-up, Renekton E Slice and Dice/Ruthless Predator damage dash, Nidalee W Pounce damage dash, Fiora Q Lunge damage dash, Camille E Hookshot stun/knock-up, Bel’Veth Q Unleashed/Rotten Tail Whip damage dash.

That is 19 champions and is the set given by Colleagues 1,2,3,5,6,8. Colleague 4 and 9 add Ornn E Orders: Dominate/Riftwalk to this set, Colleague 7 adds Shen E and Urgot E to it.

Firm exclusions that are now unanimous in Round 2:
LeBlanc W Distortion – blink with no damage/CC on arrival, damage is on recast;
Rakan W Gleaming Lantern – ally reposition teleport;
Shen E Spectral Walk/Shadow Dash – majority treats as ally reposition/teleport with no damage/CC on dash itself;
Tristana W Rocket Jump – mobility/escape;
Urgot E Needlespray – majority treats as not a travel dash;
Corki W Gatling Gun – not a dash.

Ornn E remains the main unresolved edge case. Colleagues 4 and 9 include it as a travel dash with stun/damage on arrival that can be flash-buffered; Colleagues 1,2,3,5,6,8 exclude it as not a classic travel damage/CC dash in current kit. Split ~2-7 in Round 2.

Shen/Urgot minority push in Round 2:
Colleague 10 and Colleague 7 argue Shen E is Shadow Dash taunt dash and Urgot E is Disdain flip/stun dash, therefore Flash-bufferable for the dash’s own CC arrival. Majority still treats Shen E as ally reposition/teleport and Urgot E as Needlespray/non-travel, so these remain outliers.

My current belief is unchanged in substance: the criterion is a travel dash with a travel/targeting window that ends in its own damage/CC on arrival, and Flash buffered mid-travel changes the arrival point/angle of that same dash. That supports the 19-champion core above, excludes LeBlanc/Rakan/Shen/Tristana/Urgot/Corki, and leaves Ornn E as contested but not part of the majority consensus. I am keeping Ornn out pending clearer kit consensus, and I am not adopting the Shen/Urgot taunt/dislain reinterpretation because the room majority treats them as reposition-only/non-travel under the stated “improve the dash’s own damage/CC” rule.

